s9-2-p15 = prose (cons "The adequacy premise \(\alpha\) is used when a realization *executes the represented evaluator*. A directly compiled residual can instead be related to the source term by its checked source-level conversion/path and its own machine-block evidence, without inserting the retained evaluator's machine simulation \(\nu\) as an extra proof obligation. If a mixed artifact retains an evaluator call on runtime code, that stretch uses \(\nu\) and the relevant instance of \(\alpha\). The proof dependencies are local to the realization actually used. An evaluator over raw syntax can be expressed as a guarded process, including nontermination, without a total normalizer or a universe-level collapse; typed quotation, reification, and the Futamura code equations still obey their explicit stages." nil)
